    "result_text": "Done. The change is implemented and the full suite passes (BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n**What I did:**\n\n1. **New cohesive helper** \u2014 `DisposableDomains.java`, a small self-contained class (single low-complexity method, no surrounding class complexity) that checks whether an owner's email domain is on the blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`), matching the existing pattern of sibling helpers like `EmailDuplicates` and `Households`.\n\n2. **Minimal touch to `addOwner`** \u2014 added a 3-line guard right after the owner is mapped that returns `400 BAD_REQUEST` when blocked.\n\n**Why this keeps structural impact low:** the blocklist logic lives entirely in a brand-new class with near-zero WMC_other, so it pays almost nothing. The only edit to the large `OwnerRestControllerV1` was 3 lines delegating to the helper \u2014 no new complexity added to that big class, and no existing method grown in complexity.",
